Section D records the accuracy posture for the Section Four Driver responsibilities dossier. Every knowledge fact is required to trace to its cited physical handbook page, with the cited page stating the fact. Confidence is high across the section because every rule comes from the single pinned handbook edition, and every number is spelled out in words so that the card backs read aloud exactly. The extracted text of these pages carries a font-encoding shift that garbles scattered words and turns commas into line breaks, and the point scale prints as a two-column table whose rows interleave; the dossier author decoded the shift deterministically, read each offense with the point value printed beside it, and asserts no value that stayed unreadable. Statute citations and the DMV mailing address and telephone number are not carried as learner facts. Handbook wording is paraphrased throughout; no official sentence, table, image or question is reproduced. Fines, fees and point values are stated as the pinned edition prints them; no time-variable fact beyond that edition appears, so nothing required isolation as dynamic knowledge.
